    "id": "train-7270",
    "question": "Bob is tilling a plot of his garden. The plot is 110 feet wide by 120 feet long. His tiller digs a swath two feet wide, and he can till 1 foot of ground in about 2 seconds. How long will it take him to till this plot of land, in minutes?",
    "gold": "220",
    "answer": "If Bob goes along the side that's 120 feet long, he will till 110 / 2 = 55 rows.\nEach of these rows are 120 feet long, so he will push the tiller a total of 120 * 55 = <<120*55=6600>>6,600 feet.\nHe tills 1 linear foot of ground every 2 seconds, so it will take him 2 * 6,600 = 13,200 seconds to till this plot\n13,200 seconds is 13,2000 / 60 = <<13200/60=220>>220 minutes\n#### 220"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how long it will take Bob to till the plot of land, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total area of the plot:**\n   The plot is 110 feet wide by 120 feet long.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\text{width} \\times \\text{length} = 110 \\, \\text{feet} \\times 120 \\, \\text{feet} = 13200 \\, \\text{square feet}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the area tilled by the tiller in one pass:**\n   The tiller digs a swath two feet wide.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area per pass} = \\text{width of swath} \\times \\text{length of plot} = 2 \\, \\text{feet} \\times 120 \\, \\text{feet} = 240 \\, \\text{square feet}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of passes needed to till the entire plot:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of passes} = \\frac{\\text{Total area}}{\\text{Area per pass}} = \\frac{13200 \\, \\text{square feet}}{240 \\, \\text{square feet per pass}} = 55 \\, \\text{passes}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the time to till one pass:**\n   Bob can till 1 foot of ground in about 2 seconds.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time per pass} = 2 \\, \\text{seconds per foot} \\times 120 \\, \\text{feet} = 240 \\, \\text{seconds}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total time to till the entire plot:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total time} = \\text{Number of passes} \\times \\text{Time per pass} = 55 \\, \\text{passes} \\times 240 \\, \\text{seconds per pass} = 13200 \\, \\text{seconds}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Convert the total time from seconds to minutes:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total time in minutes} = \\frac{13200 \\, \\text{seconds}}{60 \\, \\text{seconds per minute}} = 220 \\, \\text{minutes}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total time it will take Bob to till the plot of land is \\(\\boxed{220}\\) minutes.",
